---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Drug Dose by Weight" activeSlug="drug-dose">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">MedKit</a> / Calculators / <span>Drug Dose by Weight</span></div>
  <h1>Drug Dose by Weight</h1>
  <p class="cat-desc">Weight-based dosing (mg/kg) with a maximum-dose guard.</p>

  <div class="tool-ui">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="field">
        <label>Weight (kg)</label>
        <input id="wt" type="number" value="60" min="0" step="0.1" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label>Dose (mg/kg)</label>
        <input id="perkg" type="number" value="10" min="0" step="0.1" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="field">
        <label>Max dose (mg, optional)</label>
        <input id="maxd" type="number" placeholder="e.g. 500" min="0" step="1" />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label>Concentration (mg/mL, optional)</label>
        <input id="conc" type="number" placeholder="e.g. 50" min="0" step="0.1" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <button class="btn" id="calc">Calculate</button>
    <div class="result" id="out">Enter weight and dose per kg.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="article">
    <h2>Free Online Weight-Based Drug Dose Calculator</h2>
    <p>Paediatric and many adult medications are dosed per kilogram of body weight. This calculator multiplies the prescribed mg/kg by the patient's weight and, if you enter a maximum dose, caps the result to prevent overdose.</p>
    <p><code>Dose (mg) = weight(kg) × dose(mg/kg)</code> &nbsp;→&nbsp; capped at max if provided.</p>
    <p>If you enter a concentration, the required volume is also shown: <code>Volume (mL) = Dose(mg) ÷ Concentration(mg/mL)</code></p>
    <div class="callout danger">This tool performs arithmetic only. Always verify against the prescriber's order, your institution protocol, and the drug monograph before administration. Round to appropriate syringe precision.</div>
    <h3>FAQ</h3>
    <details class="faq"><summary>Why set a maximum dose?</summary><div class="body">Many drugs have a ceiling dose regardless of weight (e.g. to avoid toxicity in larger patients). The guard stops the calculation exceeding that ceiling.</div></details>
    <details class="faq"><summary>Should I use ideal or actual body weight?</summary><div class="body">It depends on the drug and protocol. Some agents use actual body weight, others use ideal or adjusted body weight. Follow local guidance.</div></details>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    const out = document.getElementById('out');
    function run() {
      const wt = parseFloat(document.getElementById('wt').value);
      const perkg = parseFloat(document.getElementById('perkg').value);
      const maxd = parseFloat(document.getElementById('maxd').value);
      const conc = parseFloat(document.getElementById('conc').value);
      if (!wt || !perkg) { out.textContent = 'Enter weight and dose per kg.'; return; }
      let dose = wt * perkg;
      let capped = false;
      if (maxd && dose > maxd) { dose = maxd; capped = true; }
      let html = `<span class="big">${dose.toFixed(1)}</span> mg`;
      if (capped) html += ` <span class="tag tag-warn">capped at max</span>`;
      if (conc) html += `<br/><span style="font-size:15px">= ${(dose / conc).toFixed(2)} mL at ${conc} mg/mL</span>`;
      out.innerHTML = html;
    }
    document.getElementById('calc').addEventListener('click', run);
    ['wt','perkg','maxd','conc'].forEach((id) => document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input', run));
    run();
  </script>
</Base>
